// Zero-argument readers of block 0's row, for `then` (docs/TESTS.md: a check
// takes no parameters, and cfg_term/cfg_succ/cfg_alt/cfg_expr all take a
// block number). The setters and terminator-writers below are exercised on
// block 0 of whatever the given built, and their only other observable
// effect (sset/lset) is a builtin, so a `then calls` cannot see it either.
term0() {
  string kind = cfg_term(0);
} return string kind;
given cfg_body_fixture ():("end")
given cond_body_fixture ():("cond")

succ0() {
  int nxt = cfg_succ(0);
} return int nxt;
given cond_body_fixture ():(1)
given cfg_body_fixture ():(-1)

alt0() {
  int alt = cfg_alt(0);
} return int alt;
given cond_body_fixture ():(2)
given cfg_body_fixture ():(-1)
